  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Healthy Islands Transformation Project-FMRF</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed PHIT project aims to address rising health challenges in Fiji and across several Pacific Islands Countries through a coordinated response, with a focus on the non-communicable disease crisis. The PHIT project finances solutions to respond to systemic and functional challenges through sequenced investments across key enablers - health infrastructure including tertiary and rural health facilities, workforce transformation, digital health and continuity of care. These investments will promote standardized learning materials for the health workforce, a regionally tailored AI-driven diagnostic tool, integrated telehealth hubs, a specialized regional hospital and training facility with expanded capacity to meet regional needs and standardized approaches to upgrading, equipping, and climate proofing facilities.</narrative>
  </description>
